    "explanation": "The governing measurement is not in dispute, and it decides this case on POL-RD-01's threshold. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the field that governs, and the trace reads 11.5 km against the booking-time optimal of 10.0 km — an excess of 1.5 km, or 15.0% of optimal (both advocates adopt these figures, and the derived deviation carries them). POL-RD-01 establishes a route deviation only where the excess is BOTH greater than 20% of optimal (2.0 km here) AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms. The absolute limb passes at 1.5 km; the percentage limb fails at 15.0% against a 20% gate, and the clause is explicit that the two limbs are conjunctive and that if either establishment test fails there is no deviation and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. So the outcome is NO_ACTION and the present state of the charge stands.\n\nTo the rider: I have not discounted your measurement. The trace is unimpaired — 133 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage, zero gaps, maximum inter-fix gap 0.0 s — so it does not engage POL-RD-07(a)–(c) and it is admitted at its full admissibility weight of 1.0; there is nothing to down-weight and no POL-RD-10(3) data failure. Your 1.5 km is real, and it is simply below the gate the policy sets. Your alternative request — run the POL-RD-02 arithmetic — cannot run: POL-RD-02 applies only where a deviation is first established under POL-RD-01, and none is. The figure you arrive at (charged_total 19.39 less a recomputed fare of 17.70 = 1.69, rounded up to 1.70) is the correct arithmetic for a deviation that the threshold test has not found. Your further request that the SGD 1.69 be held for a human reviewer under POL-RD-10 is declined because no POL-RD-10 trigger fires: identifiers and timestamps match across the artifacts, the trace is unimpaired, no exculpatory clause is asserted against an absent artifact, no fare line lacks a counterpart, and no two admissible artifacts are in mutually contradictory balance. The one gap in the record is the traffic-advisory slot EV-ADVIS-09112-01 (status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0). Its absence is citable and is cited: it means no POL-RD-03 closure exoneration is available. But an advisory could not have moved the 11.5 km trace or the 10.0 km optimal — the 15% figure would be the same with a full advisory in the pool — so its absence creates no uncertainty about the test this case turns on. That is a question for the record's completeness, not a reason to hold the charge.\n\nTo the driver: the rider's evidence fails the threshold on its own terms, so nothing further is needed from you. Your counter-statement that you 'stayed on ordinary through roads and made no additional stop' carries no evidence ID and therefore no weight under POL-RD-08; it is not relied on, and it does not need to be, because the outcome rests on the rider's own unimpaired trace. No exculpatory clause is engaged: there is no amendment re-quote (POL-RD-05: pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null), the vehicle is RYDE_X rather than RYDE_POOL so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply, and POL-RD-04's rider-detour test cannot be run (the single chat message is the rider's own mid-trip remark, naming no place or road, with a null waypoint_hint).\n\nNo clause produces a referral, and none produces a payment. POL-RD-06 is not engaged: a 15.0%/1.5 km excess is not a MATERIAL deviation (neither greater than 50% of optimal nor greater than 8.0 km), and the driver's profile shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 against 610 completed trips, so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises. POL-RD-09(4) is not engaged: the fare breakdown charges no ERP gantries and applies no airport surcharge, so there is no phantom line to refund as a billing-integrity correction. No driver compensation arises either: the billed distance (11.5 km) equals the trace distance, so there is no unbilled shortfall under POL-RD-04. The driver's profile fields cited (deviation_flags_90d, completed_trips_90d) were used only for the POL-RD-06 test, and the rider's context-only counters (prior_no_show_flags, prior_disputes_filed, prior_disputes_upheld) carried no finding against her.",
